{"header.scss removed .panel { float: right; } and replaced it with flex-only alignment (margin-left: auto), but the server-rendered header partial nests .title and .panel inside a Bootstrap .row (float grid), not a flex container, so the panel will no longer right-align in the server-rendered header": 0.0973525121808052, "The align-items() mixin includes -ms-align-items: $alignment which is not a valid Microsoft vendor-prefixed property and will be silently ignored by all browsers, while the correct -ms-flex-align is already present in the same mixin": 0.110350601375103, "Ember header uses clearfix class on .contents which is now a flex container, causing .clearfix::before/::after pseudo-elements (with display: table) to become flex items and potentially distort header alignment/spacing": 0.40763434767723083, "The order() mixin passes the same $val to both -webkit-box-ordinal-group (1-based indexing) and standard CSS order (0-based indexing), causing off-by-one error in old WebKit browsers (Safari < 6.1, Chrome < 21)": 0.7316418886184692}